<title>FRANCE: Capital of France's Brittany to get own metro.</title>
<headline>Capital of France's Brittany to get own metro.</headline>
<dateline>RENNES, France 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French authorities gave the green light on Friday for an underground railway to be built in Rennes, the capital of Brittany.</p>
<p>Rennes, which has 200,000 people, will be among the world's smallest cities to have a metro system.</p>
<p>Local officials said the 8.5 km (5.3 mile) line would cost 2.94 billion francs ($590 million). Work was expected to start next January and be completed in 2001.</p>
</text>
